<title>UK: ICO coffee exports down in Sept, but up yr/yr.</title>
<headline>ICO coffee exports down in Sept, but up yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Coffee Organisation (ICO) exporting members' exports fell to 4.84 million 60-kg bags in September from 5.46 million in August and 5.82 million in September 1995, ICO figures showed on Tuesday.</p>
<p>In the just-ended coffee year to end-September total exports by exporting members to all destinations were 71.706 million bags, up from 65.067 million a year earlier.  </p>
<p>Latest ICO export data, in thousand bags, included --</p>
<p>		 Sept 96    Sept 95    Oct/Sept 96     Oct/Sept 95</p>
<p>TOTAL	    4,844	5,816	71,706	    65,067</p>
<p>Brazil	   1,298	1,543	12,574	    16,568</p>
<p>Colombia	   680	  710	10,746	     9,342</p>
<p>Guatemala	   98	  282	 3,705	     3,564</p>
<p>Mexico		92	  101	 4,582	     3,257</p>
<p>Indonesia	  476	  501	 5,394	     3,142</p>
<p>Ivory Coast	226	  215	 2,649	     2,252</p>
<p>Uganda	     144	  284	 3,976	     2,792</p>
<p>Vietnam	    133	  223	 3,654	     3,206</p>
<p>Costa Rica	 219	  125	 2,416	     1,897</p>
<p>El Salvador	152	  161	 2,232	     1,659</p>
<p>India		218	  282	 2,636	     2,069</p>
<p>Peru		 154	  183	 1,882	     1,148</p>
<p>-- Jalil Hamid, London newsroom +44 171 542 4985</p>
